when i was a kid a million years ago one  of my favorite childhood movies that  scared the heck out of me was the  witches  [Music]  yeah this was a kid's movie so when i  heard hbo max was remaking it with the  director of back to the future  i was like we're sending you back to the  future  and i thought it would be fun to see all  the crazy differences between the 1990  original and the  2020 remake in this video we'll be  taking a look at both versions to see  what sets them apart and  don't worry if you haven't read the book  i haven't either because i can't read  but before we begin  take a moment to smash that like and  subscribe button to prevent child  cruelty and right off the bat  our first big difference is how the  story starts in the original  it's the grandmother who narrates  warning us of the evils of witches  telling us a story about a young girl  who was trapped by a witch in a painting  this story scared me so much as a kid i  went around the house looking to see if  any of the people in our paintings move  the 2020 version not only skips this  story but replaces it with one  entirely new showing us how  grandmother's friend alice was turned  into a chicken by the grand high witch  when she was a child another huge  difference from the original is  who narrates this intro it's not grandma  but our hero mouse  all grown up voiced by chris rock and  we'll get into why they made that  decision a little bit later on in the  video  both stories center around a young boy  in the original he's called luke but the  remake he's simply called hero boy  unlike the original heroboy is actually  involved in the car crash that kills his  parents spurring his grandmother to come  and take care of him  whereas in the original luke is babysat  by his grandmother while his parents go  off to a fancy dinner and get in a crash  in fact in the remake we never even see  his parents  there are also some drastic changes when  it comes to time and location the remake  opting to set the story in 1968  alabama near the gulf of mexico the  hotel where they meet the witches is  called the grand orleans imperial island  hotel while the original starts in  norway then moves to england the  majority of it taking place at a hotel  called the excelsior its time period is  never disclosed in the film but it's  safe to say  it's set anywhere from 1983 the date the  book was published to 1990 the year the  film came out  in the original we see luke spend about  one scene where he's sad about the death  of his parents whereas in the remake  it's a whole part of establishing his  relationship  with his grandmother she's the one who  gets him out of his sadness even making  him some delicious cornbread which he  says is  just like a cake and i can't help but  think that's a fun nod to the cake  grandma bakes luke and the original the  remake also heavily uses music from the  era to better situate ourselves in the  time something the original doesn't use  it all likely because it's supposed to  be set sometime  fairly modern another great difference  is our introduction of the first  witch in the original she tries to lure  luke down from his tree fort by offering  him candy and the opportunity to see her  snake  because what little boy doesn't like  snakes in the remake we meet this witch  in the general store but she's quickly  scared off by grandma  and this leads to one of the biggest  differences in the two films how they  end up at the hotel  in the original grandma gets diabetes  and they think it would be fun to take  some much needed rest at a swanky  seaside hotel  the new version i think does a better  job here with the grandmother finding  out a witches after her grandson so they  should get away for a bit in an effort  to shake her off she says once a witch  comes into your life  it never leaves you which is something  never mentioned in the original now the  grandma here also comes down with some  sort of illness which is seen through  her cough but grandma explains that's  likely a curse the witch put on her and  it eventually goes away  in both versions the boy receives a pet  mouse but where it goes from there  changes entirely in the original he gets  two mice william and mary and they  aren't that integral to the story in  fact when luke and bruno turn into mice  they can't talk to them in the remake  however there is only one mouse daisy  and they can talk to her because she  like them was transformed into a mouse  by a witch her real name is  mary a nod to one of luke's mice in the  original at the hotel we meet the owners  one you may recognize as stanley tucci  who also worked with anne hathaway in  the devil wears prada and the other  rowan atkinson or as you may know him mr  bean their roles are largely the same  however there's this totally weird  subplot in the original where mr bean is  boinking one of the maids which  somehow didn't make it into the remake  come on i thought this was hbo  and here we can just see the difference  in the signage for the members of the  international society for the prevention  of cruelty to children they get these  creepy ass mannequins while the original  gets this small sign  it's here we have our first sighting of  the grand high witch and there are a ton  of differences between anne hathaway's  version  and angelica houston's although both  have a distinctly european  accent their physical features and  powers vary drastically  fun fact it's heavily implied the grand  high witch is norwegian  as legends say she was hatched on the  frozen tundra of norway as a matter of  fact the beginning of the original has  credits over the frozen norwegian  mountains you'll notice the witches here  wear  fancy high heels when in the original  it's explicitly stated they wear plain  shoes to make it more comfortable for  their deformed feet  they have no toes their hands although  in both versions covered by gloves  differ in what's underneath and  hathaway's witch has deformed  three-finger claws while in the original  the witch's hands are usually just warty  and gross  now even though they totally power up  the grand high witch in the remake i  gotta go with the original here for the  sheer practical effects  it's a giant transformation that took  hours of makeup and prosthetics and it's  super creepy it also shows us just how  different the grand high witch is from  the others you'll also notice this  green smoke used in the original which  they've turned to purple in the remake  along with anne hathaway's joker-like  smile she has super strength powers the  ability to extend her hands  and the biggest change levitation yeah  she totally flies around the conference  room i see how they couldn't do  this in the original i mean imagine  watching this thing fly around the  difference here between  practical and computer generated effects  also extends to the mice there's just a  charm to practical effects which i love  in the original they use a combination  of real mice and prosthetics to make the  mice talk but the remake is all cgi  in the original luke manages to escape  the conference room and there's this  hilarious chase sequence where the grand  eye witch pushes a baby carriage down a  cliff to murder it don't worry it  survives but luke is later captured when  he returns to the hotel while the remake  makes it really simple and the boy is  discovered while watching bruno being  turned into a mouse  again i prefer the practical effects  here of bruno but let me know what you  like in the comments below  as the boy bruno and daisy make their  escape the high witch extends her hands  which are  cut by a fan a scene that never happens  in the original they eventually make  their way to grandma and are able to  steal a vial of the potion which turns  people into mice in the original the  vials are hidden in a book  but the remake has them out in the open  chilling in ice buckets the original  also has a scene where luke is  almost killed by the witch's cat and i'm  glad they took this out as they saved  this  for a new act 3 which i'll get into in a  bit it's here near the end of the film  that the  two versions start to differ extremely  the finale in the original sees the  witches  including the grand high witch eat the  potion lace soup  and all of them turn into mice even the  grand high witch turns into this  ugly thing the soups themselves are  totally different the original opting  for a fine crest soup while their remake  goes for a split pee  one character who i think has two or  three lines in the remake is bruno's dad  mr  jenkins in the original he's a much  larger character with his own scenes  and it's even hinted at that he's a  cheater and he continually makes  advances on the grand high witch  no wonder they left that out now we're  coming up to what i think is the biggest  difference of the two films  the grand hi which doesn't eat her soup  like she does in the original  paving the way to an entirely new ending  in which the mice and grandma have to  take her on  one on one and i actually kinda like it  since they use the mousetraps which they  set up earlier in the film to catapult  the boy over the witch's head  throwing the potion in her mouth and not  only that she turns into this hideous  rat  there's a cool chase sequence with all  these mouse traps going off and she's  eventually put in a see-through ice  bucket similar to what she's trapped in  in the original how she dies however is  totally different as she is eaten or at  least  attacked by her own cat off screen the  original film ends with luke going home  as a mouse  without bruno and one of the witches  becoming a good witch  turns him back into a boy the remake  however goes in a completely different  direction similar to the book and that  the mice  never get turned back to their original  form bruno daisy and the boys spend  their remaining years teaching other  kids about witches  grandma takes the money from the high  witch's trunk to take them on trips  around the world  and another difference is this notebook  found in the chest  in the original it contains names of all  the witches living in america but the  remake has it as all the witches living  in the world now i know i glossed over  some of the more obvious or  obscure differences but i want to know  what you thought of these two  films does this remake surpass the  original or does the original still  reign supreme thanks for watching  everyone be sure to like and subscribe  and share and come and follow me on  twitter and instagram at thingstoryt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much

